#  Electricity Bill Calculator

##  About the Project

Electricity Bill Calculator is a Python-based mini project that calculates an electricity bill based on the number of units consumed.

The project uses slab-based billing and applies different rates according to the electricity units.

##  Features

- Takes customer name as input
- Takes electricity units as input
- Validates negative units
- Calculates bill using different unit slabs
- Displays a formatted electricity bill
- Uses conditional logic for billing calculation

##  Billing Slabs

| Units | Rate |
|------|------|
| 0 - 100 | ₹5 per unit |
| 101 - 200 | ₹7 per unit |
| 201 - 300 | ₹10 per unit |
| Above 300 | ₹12 per unit |

> Note: These rates are used for this practice project and are not based on any specific electricity board tariff.

